{%- if section.settings.floating_footer -%}
  <style>
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      padding-block-end: var(--container-gutter);
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

<style>
  {%- comment -%}
  The "Links" and "Social menu" block titles render with .subheading, which has its own
  (typically smaller/uppercase) type scale. Force just the size/line-height back to Body Text
  - via --text-base, which already carries its own mobile and desktop values - so the titles
  match body copy on every breakpoint. Covers the desktop <p class="subheading"> and the
  mobile collapsible's <summary class="accordion__summary subheading">.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__block--links .subheading,
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__block--social_menu .subheading {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--text-line-height);
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  Compact mobile row for the "Collapse on mobile" social menu (see the social_menu case above):
  same links as the desktop list, laid out horizontally instead of stacked, with the network
  name hidden the accessible way (still readable by screen readers, just not shown) since the
  icon alone carries it visually here. Spans the full block-list width (like a full-width
  accordion block would) so justify-content: space-between can spread the icons edge to edge
  across the whole section instead of just its own grid column.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media screen and (max-width: 699px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__block--social_menu:has(.footer-social-menu--compact) {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer-social-menu--compact .footer-social-menu__list {
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer-social-menu--compact .footer-social-menu__text {
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border-width: 0;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    padding: 0;
    position: absolute;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  Vertical padding: same container-gutter + 0.5rem formula as sections/reviews.liquid and
  sections/faq.liquid, same on mobile and desktop, replacing this section's own fixed 2.8rem.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__content {
    padding-block: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  Lateral padding: .footer__content sits inside .footer > .container, which already insets it
  from the card's edges via its own margin (the site-wide gutter). Adding a second, separate
  padding layer here (as a previous version of this rule did) stacked on top of that margin and
  visibly doubled the side spacing. Instead, bump that same margin layer by the same +0.5rem
  the other sections use, so there's only ever one layer of side spacing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer > .container {
    --container-gutter-context: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  Newsletter: drop the outer box border - keep only the thin divider .newsletter-input-group already
  puts between the email field and the submit button. Also force the button label's color to
  --input-text-color, the color the input's own background (--input-background) is specifically
  designed to contrast with (same pair .input already uses in theme.css), instead of letting it
  inherit the footer's general text color, which isn't guaranteed to read well against
  --input-background if a merchant sets them close to each other.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .newsletter-input-group {
    border: none;
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .newsletter-input-group .link {
    color: rgb(var(--input-text-color));
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  Copyright / custom-text row: full section width, so left/right actually reads against the whole
  footer. Fixed layout now - copyright pinned start, custom text pinned end, same on mobile and
  desktop (no longer driven by an alignment setting) - muted via opacity, and the same
  container-gutter + 0.5rem vertical padding as .footer__content (see above) instead of its own
  fixed 1.5rem/2.5rem.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__copyright {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    column-gap: 0.75rem;
    row-gap: 0.25rem;
    width: 100%;
    padding-block: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  {%- comment -%} When the aside row is also present, it keeps its top padding but drops the bottom one so the two rows don't double up. {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__aside:has(+ .footer__copyright) {
    padding-block-end: 0;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
  Payment icons: theme.css positions .footer__aside's children differently depending on how many
  are present (justify-content: space-between with 2, a 3-column grid with 3 - see .footer__aside
  in theme.css), so the payment icons row shifts horizontally depending on whether the locale
  selector and/or social icons are also shown. Pulling it onto its own full-width row and
  centering it there keeps it in the same horizontal spot regardless of its siblings.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .footer__payment-icons {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    justify-content: center;
  }
</style>

<div class="footer {% if section.settings.floating_footer %}footer--floating{% endif %} color-scheme color-scheme--{{ section.settings.color_scheme.id }}" {% if section.settings.floating_footer %}style="border-radius: {{ section.settings.footer_border_radius }}px;"{% endif %}>
  <div class="container">
    {%- assign scrolling_logo_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'scrolling_logo' | first -%}

    {%- capture scrolling_logo -%}
      {%- assign logo_image = scrolling_logo_block.settings.image -%}

      {%- if logo_image != blank -%}
        {%- if scrolling_logo_block.settings.layout == 'full_width' -%}
          <div class="footer__big-logo footer__big-logo--full" {{ scrolling_logo_block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {{- logo_image | image_url: width: logo_image.width | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '200,400,600,800,1000,1200,1400,1600,1800,2000,2200,2400,2600,2800,3000,3200' -}}
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
        <marquee-text speed="0.3" direction="start-to-end" class="footer__big-logo footer__big-logo--scrolling scrolling-content full-bleed" {{ scrolling_logo_block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <div class="scrolling-content__item" style="--scrolling-content-gap: 80px">
            {%- capture style_attribute -%}--image-mobile-max-width: {{ scrolling_logo_block.settings.mobile_image_width }}vw; --image-max-width: {{ scrolling_logo_block.settings.image_width }}vw;{%- endcapture -%}
            {{- logo_image | image_url: width: logo_image.width | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', style: style_attribute, class: 'constrained-image', widths: '200,400,600,800,1000,1200,1400,1600,1800,2000' -}}
          </div>
        </marquee-text>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    <div class="footer__content">
      {%- if section.blocks.first.type == 'scrolling_logo' -%}
        {{- scrolling_logo -}}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%}
        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        FOOTER BLOCKS (MAIN CONTENT)
        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        {%- endcomment -%}

        <div class="footer__block-list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- comment -%}
            Set to true by the branches that actually render a mobile <details> accordion, so the
            footer__block--accordion-links wrapper class below stays in sync with the real collapse state.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign block_collapses_on_mobile = false -%}
            {%- capture block_content -%}
              {%- case block.type -%}
                {%- when '@app' -%}
                  {%- render block -%}
                  
                {%- when 'image' -%}
                  {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                    {%- capture sizes -%}{{ block.settings.image_width }}px{%- endcapture -%}
                    {%- capture widths -%}{{ block.settings.image_width }}, {{ block.settings.image_width | times: 2 | at_most: block.settings.image.width }}{%- endcapture -%}
                    {%- capture style -%}--image-max-width: {{ block.settings.image_width }}px{%- endcapture -%}

                    {%- if block.settings.link != blank -%}
                      <a href="{{ block.settings.link }}">
                        {{- block.settings.image | image_url: width: block.settings.image.width | image_tag: sizes: sizes, widths: widths, style: style, class: 'constrained-image' -}}
                      </a>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{- block.settings.image | image_url: width: block.settings.image.width | image_tag: sizes: sizes, widths: widths, style: style, class: 'constrained-image' -}}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endif -%}

                {%- when 'text' -%}
                  {%- if block.settings.title != blank or block.settings.content != blank or shop.features.follow_on_shop? and block.settings.enable_follow_on_shop -%}
                    <div class="v-stack gap-4.5">
                      {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                        <p class="subheading">{{ block.settings.title }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}

                      {%- if block.settings.content != blank -%}
                        <div class="prose">
                          {{- block.settings.content -}}
                        </div>
                      {%- endif -%}

                      {%- if shop.features.follow_on_shop? and block.settings.enable_follow_on_shop -%}
                        <div class="follow-on-shop">
                          {{- shop | login_button: action: 'follow' -}}
                        </div>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}

                {%- when 'links' -%}
                  {%- assign menu = block.settings.menu -%}

                  {%- if menu != blank and menu.links.size > 0 -%}
                    {%- assign menu_title = block.settings.menu_title | default: menu.title -%}

                    {%- capture menu_content -%}
                      <ul class="v-stack gap-2.5 unstyled-list" role="list">
                        {%- for link in menu.links -%}
                          <li>
                            <a href="{{ link.url }}" class="link-reversed link-tap-area">{{ link.title }}</a>
                          </li>
                        {%- endfor -%}
                      </ul>
                    {%- endcapture -%}

                    <div class="v-stack gap-4.5 {% if block.settings.collapse_on_mobile %}sm-max:hidden{% endif %}">
                      {%- if block.settings.show_menu_title -%}
                        <p class="subheading">{{ menu_title }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}

                      {{- menu_content -}}
                    </div>

                    {%- if block.settings.collapse_on_mobile -%}
                      {%- assign block_collapses_on_mobile = true -%}
                      {%- render 'accordion', title: menu_title, content: menu_content, subheading_title: true, class: 'sm:hidden' -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endif -%}

                {%- when 'social_menu' -%}
                  {%- assign social_menu = block.settings.menu -%}

                  {%- if social_menu != blank and social_menu.links.size > 0 -%}
                    {%- comment -%} Icon color: captured once here and applied below directly on the <span> that wraps ONLY the icon (never the <a> or the text), so it cannot affect the link text under any circumstance. {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- capture icon_style -%}
                      {%- if block.settings.icon_color != blank and block.settings.icon_color != 'rgba(0,0,0,0)' -%}color: rgb({{ block.settings.icon_color.rgb }});{%- endif -%}
                    {%- endcapture -%}
                    {%- assign icon_style = icon_style | strip -%}

                    {%- capture social_menu_content -%}
                      <ul class="footer-social-menu__list v-stack gap-2.5 unstyled-list" role="list">
                        {%- for link in social_menu.links -%}
                          {%- liquid
                            # Detect the network from the URL first (most reliable), falling back to the link text
                            assign link_url_downcase = link.url | downcase
                            assign link_title_downcase = link.title | downcase
                            assign social_icon = blank

                            if link_url_downcase contains 'instagram.com' or link_title_downcase contains 'instagram'
                              assign social_icon = 'instagram'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains 'youtube.com' or link_url_downcase contains 'youtu.be' or link_title_downcase contains 'youtube'
                              assign social_icon = 'youtube'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains 'tiktok.com' or link_title_downcase contains 'tiktok'
                              assign social_icon = 'tiktok'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains 'pinterest.com' or link_title_downcase contains 'pinterest'
                              assign social_icon = 'pinterest'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains 'facebook.com' or link_title_downcase contains 'facebook'
                              assign social_icon = 'facebook'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains '//x.com' or link_url_downcase contains '.x.com' or link_url_downcase contains 'twitter.com' or link_title_downcase contains 'twitter'
                              assign social_icon = 'twitter'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains 'linkedin.com' or link_title_downcase contains 'linkedin'
                              assign social_icon = 'linkedin'
                            elsif link_url_downcase contains 'whatsapp.com' or link_url_downcase contains 'wa.me' or link_title_downcase contains 'whatsapp'
                              assign social_icon = 'whatsapp'
                            endif
                          -%}

                          <li class="footer-social-menu__item">
                            {%- comment -%} link.type == 'http_link' is Shopify's own signal for an externally-entered URL {%- endcomment -%}
                            <a href="{{ link.url }}" class="footer-social-menu__link link-reversed link-tap-area" {% if link.type == 'http_link' %}target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}>
                              <span class="footer-social-menu__icon-wrap shrink-0" {% if icon_style != blank %}style="{{ icon_style }}"{% endif %}>
                                {%- if social_icon != blank -%}
                                  {%- render 'icon' with social_icon, width: block.settings.icon_width, mobile_width: block.settings.mobile_icon_width, class: 'footer-social-menu__icon' -%}
                                {%- else -%}
                                  {%- comment -%} Generic fallback icon so unmatched links never break the layout {%- endcomment -%}
                                  {%- render 'icon' with 'picto-social-media', width: block.settings.icon_width, mobile_width: block.settings.mobile_icon_width, class: 'footer-social-menu__icon' -%}
                                {%- endif -%}
                              </span>
                              <span class="footer-social-menu__text">{{- link.title -}}</span>
                            </a>
                          </li>
                        {%- endfor -%}
                      </ul>
                    {%- endcapture -%}

                    {%- comment -%}
                    Unlike the 'links' block, "Collapse on mobile" here isn't a <details> accordion - hiding
                    social icons behind a tap defeats the point of showing them. Instead, on mobile it swaps
                    the title + vertical icon/text list for a compact, centered, icon-only row (no title, no
                    network names).
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- assign social_collapse_on_mobile = block.settings.collapse_on_mobile -%}

                    <div class="footer-social-menu v-stack gap-4.5 {% if social_collapse_on_mobile %}sm-max:hidden{% endif %}">
                      {%- if block.settings.show_menu_title and block.settings.heading != blank -%}
                        <p class="subheading footer-social-menu__heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}

                      {{- social_menu_content -}}
                    </div>

                    {%- if social_collapse_on_mobile -%}
                      <div class="footer-social-menu--compact sm:hidden">
                        {{- social_menu_content -}}
                      </div>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endif -%}

                {%- when 'newsletter' -%}
                  <div class="v-stack gap-4.5">
                    {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                      <p class="subheading">{{ block.settings.title }}</p>
                    {%- endif -%}

                    <div class="v-stack gap-5.5">
                      {%- if block.settings.content != blank -%}
                        <div class="prose">
                          {{- block.settings.content -}}
                        </div>
                      {%- endif -%}

                      <div class="v-stack gap-4">
                        {%- render 'newsletter-form', id: section.id -%}

                        {%- if block.settings.disclaimer_text != blank -%}
                          <div class="prose text-subdued text-sm">
                            {{- block.settings.disclaimer_text -}}
                          </div>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

              {%- endcase -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}

            {%- if block_content != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
              footer__block--accordion-links drives the mobile stacked-accordion spacing - applied only when
              the block actually rendered a mobile accordion above (see block_collapses_on_mobile).
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="footer__block footer__block--{{ block.type | remove_first: '@' }} {% if block_collapses_on_mobile %}footer__block--accordion-links{% endif %}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {{- block_content -}}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.blocks.first.type != 'scrolling_logo' -%}
        {{- scrolling_logo -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    FOOTER ASIDE (COPYRIGHT + LOCALIZATION SELECTORS + PAYMENT METHODS)
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign show_locale_selector = false
      assign show_country_selector = false

      if section.settings.show_locale_selector and localization.available_languages.size > 1
        assign show_locale_selector = true
      endif

      if section.settings.show_country_selector and localization.available_countries.size > 1
        assign show_country_selector = true
      endif
    -%}

    {%- capture footer_aside_content -%}
      {%- if show_locale_selector or show_country_selector -%}
        <div class="h-stack gap-5 md:justify-start">
          {%- liquid
            if show_country_selector
              render 'localization-selector', type: 'country', show_country_name: section.settings.show_country_name, show_country_flag: section.settings.show_country_flag
            endif

            if show_locale_selector
              render 'localization-selector', type: 'locale'
            endif
          -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_social_media -%}
        {%- render 'social-media' -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_payment_icons and shop.enabled_payment_types.size > 0 -%}
        <ul class="footer__payment-icons h-stack gap-4 wrap unstyled-list">
          {%- for type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}
            <li>{{- type | payment_type_svg_tag -}}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- comment -%}
    Copyright + custom text: their own full-width row below the aside, so it spans the whole footer
    instead of just the width of the copyright text. Copyright pinned start, custom text pinned end
    (see .footer__copyright in the <style> above) - both sit on one line (flex row) and wrap only if
    there isn't room.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture footer_copyright_content -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_copyright or section.settings.footer_bottom_text != blank -%}
        <div class="footer__copyright">
          {%- if section.settings.show_copyright -%}
            <span class="text-sm">© {{ 'now' | date: '%Y' }} - {{ shop.name }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.footer_bottom_text != blank -%}
            <span class="text-sm">{{ section.settings.footer_bottom_text }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- if footer_aside_content != blank or footer_copyright_content != blank -%}
      <hr class="separator full-bleed">

      {%- if footer_aside_content != blank -%}
        <div class="footer__aside">
          {{- footer_aside_content -}}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {{- footer_copyright_content -}}
    {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.footer.name",
  "class": "shopify-section--footer",
  "tag": "footer",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:global.colors.scheme",
      "default": "scheme-2"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "floating_footer",
      "label": "t:sections.footer.floating_footer",
      "info": "t:sections.footer.floating_footer_info",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "footer_border_radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.footer.footer_border_radius",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.floating_footer }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_social_media",
      "label": "t:sections.footer.show_social_media",
      "info": "t:sections.footer.show_social_media_info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_payment_icons",
      "label": "t:sections.footer.show_payment_icons",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_copyright",
      "label": "Show copyright",
      "info": "Also controls the divider line and bottom bar it sits in — when nothing in that row is enabled (copyright text, custom text, payment icons, social media, country/language selector), the bar is hidden entirely.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "footer_bottom_text",
      "label": "Custom text",
      "info": "Shown in the bottom bar, next to the copyright line."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:global.localization.country_region_selector_category",
      "info": "t:global.localization.country_region_selector_category_info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_country_selector",
      "label": "t:global.localization.show_country_region_selector",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_country_name",
      "label": "t:global.localization.show_country_name",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_country_selector }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_country_flag",
      "label": "t:global.localization.show_country_flag",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_country_selector }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:global.localization.language_selector_category",
      "info": "t:global.localization.language_selector_category_info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_locale_selector",
      "label": "t:global.localization.show_locale_selector",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@app"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "name": "t:sections.footer.blocks.image.name",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "t:global.image.image",
          "info": "t:sections.footer.blocks.image.image_size_recommendation"
        },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "image_width",
          "min": 50,
          "max": 300,
          "step": 10,
          "unit": "px",
          "label": "t:global.image.width",
          "default": 150
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link",
          "label": "t:global.text.link"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "name": "t:sections.footer.blocks.text.name",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "inline_richtext",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "t:global.text.heading",
          "default": "About our store"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "t:global.text.content",
          "default": "<p>Use this text area to tell your customers about your brand and vision. You can change it in the theme editor.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "enable_follow_on_shop",
          "label": "t:sections.footer.blocks.text.show_follow_on_shop",
          "info": "t:sections.footer.blocks.text.show_follow_on_shop_info",
          "default": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "links",
      "name": "t:sections.footer.blocks.links.name",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "link_list",
          "id": "menu",
          "label": "t:sections.footer.blocks.links.menu",
          "info": "t:sections.footer.blocks.links.menu_info",
          "default": "footer"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "collapse_on_mobile",
          "label": "t:sections.footer.blocks.links.collapse_on_mobile",
          "default": true
        },
        {
